    </expertiseList>
    <grid>
      <Value>
{"layout":{"Umbraco.BlockGrid":[{"contentUdi":"umb://element/e5fe2d9cf3f64798a3b1f68ecde2643d","areas":[],"columnSpan":12,"rowSpan":1}]},"contentData":[{"contentTypeKey":"9a4f7c2e-1b3d-4e8a-bf01-7d62a8f5c930","udi":"umb://element/e5fe2d9cf3f64798a3b1f68ecde2643d","content":"\u003cdiv class=\"\" data-block=\"true\" data-editor=\"758bl\" data-offset-key=\"dadl7-0-0\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"dadl7-0-0\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"_1mf _1mj\" data-offset-key=\"dadl7-0-0\"\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Western Cape is one of South Africa’s most dynamic and densely developed regions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA leader in renewable energy, urban infrastructure, and coastal engineering,the region demands precision, responsiveness, and consistent excellence from those working to support everything from city-scale roadworks to internationally-renowned energy projects.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/wqahyi5m/roadlab-western-cape-projects.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eOur far-reaching network supports projects in environments as diverse as the Western Cape itself.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe Western Cape is undergoing a significant wave of infrastructure development. \u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNew roads are linking towns and easing congestion. Wind farms are rising in the inland hills.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDams, bridges and public amenities are being expanded or rebuilt to serve growing communities and changing environmental conditions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBehind these projects is a network of municipalities, engineers, contractors and quality assurance teams working across regions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOur commercial branches in Bellville, George and Langebaan play a central role in this environment — delivering geotechnical and materials testing across Cape Town, the West Coast and beyond. \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/xf3a153j/roadlab-network.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/riipvjk2/oya-windfarm-testing.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"heading-h3\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSupporting the Western Cape’s Renewable Shift at Oya Windfarm\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Oya Wind Farm project marks a significant milestone in the Western Cape’s transition to sustainable energy. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLocated between Matjiesfontein and Sutherland, this large-scale development will host 32 Vestas 4.5 MW turbines and is expected to generate over 590 GWh of clean energy annually — enough to power more than 180,000 households.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRoadlab Bellville is supporting this landmark project with a full suite of testing services, including concrete strength testing, density testing, and material classification. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOur teams are involved in verifying foundation stability, ensuring concrete quality for long-duration pours, and monitoring compaction for turbine platforms and internal access roads.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith work spanning months and involving high-stakes logistical coordination, the Oya Windfarm reflects the kind of trusted, technical partnership Roadlab provides.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOur work here contributes to a greener, more resilient energy future for South Africa.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/xddpuuy3/roadlab-oya-windfarm-work.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/mwtd3pb2/renewable-energy-projects.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/fbzikza5/roadlab-at-oya-windfarm-for-testing.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/ymoj03i3/travel-to-work-site.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"heading-h3\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe Southern Cape: New Malls and Road Infrastructure\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt Hartenbos’ new \u003cstrong\u003eGarden Walk Mall\u003c/strong\u003e, Roadlab is working with a number of contractors to ensure compliance, compaction accuracy, and structural \u003cbr\u003eperformance across the site. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTesting includes moisture-density relationships \u003cstrong\u003e(MODS)\u003c/strong\u003e, California Bearing Ratio \u003cstrong\u003e(CBR)\u003c/strong\u003e testing, field densities, dynamic cone penetrometer \u003cstrong\u003e(DCP)\u003c/strong\u003e assessments, and \u003cstrong\u003econcrete cub\u003c/strong\u003ee strength testing.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis support is helping to ensure the safety and longevity of public spaces, parking infrastructure, and access roads at one of the Garden Route’s busiest new commercial hubs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRoadlab is also providing full quality assurance support for the \u003cstrong\u003eupgrading of Maalgate Bridge\u003c/strong\u003e — a key corridor between George and Mossel Bay.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOur teams are conducting\u003cstrong\u003e concrete cube \u003c/strong\u003etesting, \u003cstrong\u003ematerial classificatio\u003c/strong\u003en, \u003cstrong\u003easphalt verification\u003c/strong\u003e, and potential \u003cstrong\u003edurability assessments\u003c/strong\u003e to support both the new bridge and its connecting roads. \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe project will enhance regional traffic capacity and resilient road infrastructure.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/m2dpg0rz/garden-walk-mall-1.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/bcechtym/garden-walk-mall-2.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/ohydsfnm/malgate-bridge.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"heading-h3\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003eSupporting Municipal \u0026amp; \u003cbr\u003eInfrastructure Development\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe are proud to serve the City of Cape Town and municipalities of the West Coast District, Witzenberg, George and Saldanha Bay with advanced materials testing that ensures public infrastructure is safe, compliant, and built to last.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBrackenfell Parking Area\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWe are providing concrete durability and compaction testing for a high-traffic commuter zone.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGovan Mbeki Road and Jakes Gerwel Drive\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eOngoing municipal roadworks requiring continuous pavement-layer verification and subgrade strength testing.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePaarl Dal Josaphat Sport Stadium Parking\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eConcrete compliance and surface strength testing for expanded recreational infrastructure.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSir Lowry’s Pass \u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eGeotechnical and slope stability support on one of the province’s most critical transport corridors.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eClanwilliam, Wolseley Dam\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003eInfrastructure improvements linked to regional water security efforts, requiring detailed classification and concrete performance verification.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/uuqdcp5u/municipal-projects-roadlab-map.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/53fham1c/roadworks-vehicle.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/r2ycfwuy/roadwork-investigations.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/kpepdq5n/roadworks-in-western-cape.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"heading-h3\"\u003eCommitment to Quality: A SANAS-Accredited Facility\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt Roadlab, quality is what we do.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis commitment to excellence shapes how we support infrastructure development across the Western Cape — from dense urban upgrades to remote renewable energy builds.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBy continually refining our geotechnical, concrete, and materials testing processes, we help ensure that the region’s roads, bridges, coastal structures, and wind farms are built to endure.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOur work is underpinned by strict adherence to SANAS accreditation standards, ensuring that every test we perform meets national and international benchmarks for accuracy, reliability, and compliance.\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"heading-h3\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003eWe\u0027re ready to answer your questions. \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"heading-h3\"\u003eReach out below.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/0cbovclm/western-cape-construction-quality.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cimg src=\"/media/paohvimw/western-cape-construction-quality-assurance.jpg\" /\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\r\n"}],"settingsData":[]}
</Value>
    </grid>
